        Resource: !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/*'
```

**Why this is problematic**:

```
IAM Role Policy grants: s3:GetObject, s3:PutObject, s3:DeleteObject
Bucket Policy ALSO grants: s3:GetObject, s3:PutObject, s3:DeleteObject

For same-account access, only ONE of these is needed.
Having both:
1. Creates confusion in security audits (which grant is authoritative?)
2. The bucket policy grant survives even if you remove the IAM role permission
3. s3:DeleteObject in bucket policy + IAM role = double confirmation of delete ability
   on customer video content with no audit trail separation
```

```yaml
# CORRECTED - Remove AllowLambdaAccess from bucket policy entirely
# IAM role policy is sufficient for same-account access
# Keep only the two necessary statements:
BucketPolicy:
  Type: AWS::S3::BucketPolicy
  DependsOn: WebsiteDistribution
  Properties:
    Bucket: !Ref StreamingVideoBucket
    PolicyDocument:
      Version: '2012-10-17'
      Statement:
        - Sid: AllowCloudFrontOACAccess
          Effect: Allow
          Principal:
            Service: cloudfront.amazonaws.com
          Action: s3:GetObject
          Resource: !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/*'
          Condition:
            StringEquals:
              AWS:SourceArn: !Sub >-
                arn:aws:cloudfront::${AWS::AccountId}:distribution/${WebsiteDistribution}

        - Sid: DenyNonHTTPS
          Effect: Deny
          Principal: '*'
          Action: 's3:*'
          Resource:
            - !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}'
            - !Sub 'arn:aws:s3:::${StreamingVideoBucket}/*'
          Condition:
            Bool:
              aws:SecureTransport: 'false'

        # REMOVED: AllowLambdaAccess - IAM role policy handles this
        # Same-account access is controlled by IAM, bucket policy not needed
```

